<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss, Canada sign double taxation accord.</title>
<headline>Swiss, Canada sign double taxation accord.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland and Canada have signed a new double-taxation agreement that can take effect after it is ratified by parliament, the Swiss finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The accord, which replaces a 1976 treaty, mostly reflects the OECD model and Swiss contractural practice, it said.</p>
<p>It reduces withholding tax on dividends to five percent from 15 and on interest to 10 percent from 15. It also extends the list of exemptions for licensing fees.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
